@inject ApiMetadata Api
@* Tabs' Overview, written by hand after Button's: picking a tab previewed in each mode, the looks,
   vertical tabs, the tab in the address, tabs in a form, panel padding and tabs that are links.
   Parts, Accessibility and See also come from the doc comments and components.json. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Picking a tab</Heading>
<TextBlock>To set the tab that opens first, set <Code>Selected</Code>. On interactive pages, to follow the selected tab from C#, bind it with <Code>@@bind-Selected</Code>. A tab's value is its <Code>Value</Code>, or its label in lower case with dashes, such as <Code>billing-history</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-modes" />
<TextBlock>Every panel renders with the page, and picking a tab only shows another panel. Switching is instant, and it keeps what the user typed. Content that's slow to build or rarely opened is better on a page of its own, behind a <Anchor Href="docs/components/tabs#tabs-as-links">TabLink</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Variants, icons and badges</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tabs come in three variants: an underline (the default), soft tabs, or a segmented control. Set <Code>Variant</Code>. Each <Code>Tab</Code> can have an <Code>Icon</Code> and a <Code>Badge</Code>, or be <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-variants" />

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and full width</Heading>
<TextBlock>To match the buttons and fields around the tabs, set <Code>Size</Code>. To share the row equally between the tabs, set <Code>FullWidth</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-sizes" />

<Heading Level="2">Vertical</Heading>
<TextBlock>Vertical tabs sit in a column beside the panels, from 640px up. Set <Code>Orientation="Orientation.Vertical"</Code>. On phones, the tabs stay a row above the panels, which scrolls when it doesn't fit.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-vertical" />

<Heading Level="2">In the URL</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tabs can keep the selected tab in the URL, so a link to <Code>?tab=billing</Code> opens Billing, and a copied URL keeps the tab. Set <Code>QueryKey</Code>. The URL overrides <Code>Selected</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-url" />

<Heading Level="2">In a form</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tabs can split a long form. Put <Code>Tabs</Code> inside a <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>: every panel is part of the form, so every field posts.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-account-form" />
<TextBlock>When the server finds errors, the first tab with errors opens, unless the open tab has some. Each tab shows how many errors it has. This example sets <Code>NativeValidation="false"</Code> so the server's errors show.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>With the browser's own checks on, the default, the form post waits until they pass. <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">IzzyBlazor's script</Anchor> opens the tab of the first field the browser stops at, so its message shows.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Panel padding</Heading>
<TextBlock>To pad every panel on all sides, set <Code>ContentPadding</Code>. To run a table edge to edge in one panel, set that <Code>Tab</Code>'s own <Code>ContentPadding="0"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-padding" />

<Heading Level="2">Tabs as links</Heading>
<TextBlock>Tab links suit sections that are pages of their own. Use <Code>TabLink</Code> in place of <Code>Tab</Code>. The tabs are a <Code>nav</Code> of plain links, and the server marks the one for the current URL.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tabs-links" />
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>A tab stays current on the pages below its link, so a <Code>settings</Code> tab is current on <Code>settings/billing</Code> too. To stop that, set <Code>Match="NavLinkMatch.All"</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When several tabs link to one page and differ only by their query, one is current at a time.</ListItem>
</List>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Tabs Label="Account">
            <Tab Label="Profile" Icon="Lucide.User">...</Tab>
            <Tab Label="Billing" Badge="2">...</Tab>
        </Tabs>

        @* Links to pages of their own. *@
        <Tabs Label="Settings">
            <TabLink Href="settings/profile" Label="Profile" />
            <TabLink Href="settings/billing" Label="Billing" />
        </Tabs>
        """;
}
